        <head>CURED BY CUTCIURA IN THREE DAYS</head>
        <p>CURED BY CUTCIURA IN THREE DAYS</p>
        <p>Baby Cooper's case seemed hopeless. The trouble began when he was only seven weeks old— his head, face, shout- u'.s, neck and arms suddenly became red and rough. "Just the way ands .rn if Le dab.. in ater deal," said Mr. William</p>
        <p>Cooper,</p>
        <p>_ _ of the Prudential Assurance Co., Ltd., 89 Bul- wer Road, Leytonstone, N. E. "The doctor saw it was eczema, and did his best for six long months, without avail; baby went from bad to worse, the af- fected parts beeeming one solid sore. The child was a pitiable sight, crying and exhausting himself in his futile efforts to allay his torturing skin by rubbing and scratching." "It was one Friday," continued Mr. Cooper, "that we thought we would try Cuticura. Ointment. We applied it that same evening, and on the follow- ing day my wife said she noticed a change for the better. On the Monday —after three days' treatment— it was quite apparent to me that a complete cure had been effected. In a week his skin was perfectly clear. Really, I think I should never have believed it if I had not seen it myself. We were al- most despairing, thinking it meant either death of our darling, or lifelong suffering. The only word I can find to express my feelings is ' wonderful.' "</p>
