      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-03-30_WidnesExaminer_art0109" n="art0109">
        <p>This is one of our GUINEA COSTUMES Very Stylish and thororighly well Tailored. Coat has fitting back and plaited basque, to wear open or closed; body and sleeves lined good stripe; skirt has seven gores, seams lapped and stitched, and stitched round bottom. The entire garment is carefully turned out, and equal to any at twice the cost. Produced in the famous Kashmera • habit cloth, guaranteed not to spot. Colours: Light and dark navy, petunia, wine, myrtle, brown, and black. Bust measures 34, 36, 38. Skirt length, 33, 40, 42. Sent carriage paid on receipt of 21/-.</p>
        <p>A. JOHNS &amp; CO., The 'lrene.' Ladies' Tailors, Patterns of Cloths post tree. Forest Hill, London.</p>
        <p>-A-WONDERFUL DISCOVERY.</p>
        <p>This is the age of research and experitnent,when all nature so to speak, is ransacked by the scientific for the comfort and happiness of man. Science has indeed made giant strides during the past century, and among the—by no means leaA important—discoveries in medicine comes that of THERAPION.</p>
        <p>This preparation is unquestionably one of the most reliable Patent Medicines eler introduced, and has been used in the Continental Hospitals by Ricord, Rostan. Jobert, Velpeau, Maisonneuve, the well-known Chas- saignac, and indeed by all who are regarded as author- ities in such matters, including the celebrated Lalle- mand, and Roux, by whom it was some time since uniformly adopted, and that it is worthy the attention of those who require such a remedy we think there is no doubt. From the time of Aristotle downwards, a potent agsnt in the removal of these diseases has (like the famed philosopher's stone) been the object of search of some hopeful, generous minds; and far beyond the mere power—lf such could ever have been discovered—of transmuting the baser metals into gold is surely the discovery of a remedy so potent as to replenish the fail- ing energies in the one case, and in the other so effectu- ally. speedily. and safely •to expel from the system the poisons of acquired or inherited diseases in all their pro- tean forms as to leave no taint or trace behind. Such is THE NEW FRENCH REMEDY, TH ERAPION,</p>
        <p>which may certainly rank with, if not take precedence of. many of the discoveries of our day, about which no littl,s ostentation and noise have been made, and thePltensive and ever-increasing demand that has been created for this medicine appears to prove that it is destined to cast into oblivion all those questionable remedies that were formerly the sole reliance of medical men. For particulars of Therapion send stamped. addressed envelope to The Le Clerc Medicine Co., Haverstock-rd. Hampstead, London.</p>
