        <p>CHESHIRE COUNTY COUNTY COUNCIL.— EDUCATION DEPARTMENT. ADMISSION OF PUPIL TEACHERS, 1907. AN EXAMINATION will be held about the beginning of May, at various Centres in the County, for Candi- dates who will be not less than 16 years of age on August Ist, 1907, and who desire to become Pupil Teachers in the County Elementary Education Area, the Non-County Boroughs, or the Urban District of Wallasey. SCHOLARSHIPS FOR INTENDING PUPIL TEACHERS. A number of Scholarships not exceeding twenty, are offered to Boys or Girls who have attained the age of 14 years, and are not over 15 years on or before July 31st, 1907, and without having held a County Scholar- ship have been in attendance at an approved Secondary School for at least two years, if such signify their intention to become Pupil Teachers at the age of 16, or as soon as possible. lta _ For further particulars of the above Examinations, and Forms of application to enter for the same (which must be returned on or before the 13th April),apply Rd. P. WARD, , Director of Education. County Education Office, City Rd., Chester.</p>
