        <p>COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER. DISEASES OF ANIMALS ACTS, 1894 to 1903, AND THE DOGS ACT, 1906. CHESFIIRE (CONTROL OF DOGS) ORDER, 1907. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the Cheshire County Council, as the Local Authority under the Diseases of Animals Acts, 1894 to 1903, for the County of Chester, excluding the Municipal Boroughs either wholly or partly situate therein, intend at the expiration of 14 days from the date of this notice, to submit to the Board of Agriculture and Fisheries for confirmation the following REGULATIONS, made at a Meeting of the Executive Committee of such Local Authority held at Chester Castle on Thursday, the 14th day of March, 1907, viz. : CONTROL OF DOGS BETWEEN SUNSET AND SUNRISE. I.—Every dog in the district of the Local AUthority shall at all times during the period between one hour after sunset and one hour before sunrise, be kept by the -Owner thereof under control by being : (i.) Confined in a kennel or other enclosure from which it cannot escape; or (ii.) Secured to some premises by a collar and chain; or Accompanied by and under the effectual con trol of the Owner or other person in charg- thereof, such Regulations to apply to the whole of that portion Of the County under the jurisdiction of the Committee. AND NOTICE IS HEREBY FURTHER GIVEN, that a copy of such Regulations will be kept at the Office at Chester of the undersigned, the Clerk to such Council, and the same can be inspected by any of the Ratepayers of the County, without fee or reward, any day during office hours for 14 days from tbe date of the first publication of this Notice. AND NOTICE IS HEREBY ALSO FURTHER GIVEN, that copies of the said Regulations may be 9,htained at the aforesaid Office, by any Ratepayer of the County, on payment of Sixpence each. Dated this 18th day of March, 1907. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk to the Cheshire County Council. Council Offices, Northgat,e-street, Chester. CANADA BY ALL lAN E.-1 HE ACHE OF OCEAN COAFfIRT IS AT1'3.11q330 IN THE FAST T